# AGARD AR-138 (1979), Appendix B1 (V. Schmitt and F. Charpin, ONERA),
# TABLE B1-14, printed page B1-20 == PDF page 346 of
#   docs/papers/benchmark_test_cases/agard_1979_ar138_experimental_data_base.pdf
# TEST 2308:  M0 = .8395   ALPHA = 3.06   REC = 11.72*10**6
#   -- all four read from the printed page header, not from the OCR sidecar.
#
# Read from the PAGE IMAGE (pdfimages -> native 1648x2330 1-bit 200 dpi scan).
# The PDF's OCR TEXT LAYER FOR THIS PAGE CONTAINS ONLY THE HEADER AND NO TABLE BODY --
# see models/onera_m6/PROVENANCE_TABLE_B1_14.md sections 2 and 3.  NOT read from the .txt sidecar.
#
# COLUMNS (the format compare_cp.py declares it wants, cases/navier_class/M6H1/compare_cp.py
# docstring "INPUT FORMAT"):  section_id  y_over_b  surface  x_over_c  Cp
#
# section_id  : SECTION 1..7 exactly as the table's own column headers name them.
# y_over_b    : AGARD AR-138 B1 section 5.1.1, printed page B1-4 == PDF page 330, READ FROM
#               THE PAGE IMAGE: "271 pressure orifices divided in 7 sections
#               (y/b = 0.20/0.44/0.65/0.80/0.90/0.96 and 0.99)".  NOTE 0.96, NOT 0.95.
# surface     : from the SIGN OF THE TABLE'S OWN Z/L COLUMN (Z/L < 0 -> lower, Z/L >= 0 -> upper).
#               Not assumed from row order.  The one Z/L == 0 row (SECTION 4, NP 1, x/l = 0)
#               is the leading-edge orifice and is filed 'upper'; see PROVENANCE section 6.
# x_over_c    : the table's X/L column (x measured along the LOCAL chord from the local
#               leading edge -- AR-138 B1 section 8 list of symbols, PDF page 332).
# Cp          : the table's CP column for TEST 2308.
#
# ROW COUNT 271 == the orifice count AR-138 B1 section 5.1.1 states on the page ("271 pressure
# orifices"), reached independently by segmenting the page: 4 x 34 + 3 x 45 = 271.
#
# HOW EVERY DIGIT WAS CROSS-CHECKED, AND WHAT IS STILL UNRESOLVED:
#   see models/onera_m6/PROVENANCE_TABLE_B1_14.md.  Summary:
#   - x_over_c and Cp were each read TWICE INDEPENDENTLY (a human read of magnified page crops,
#     and a template classifier trained ONLY on this page's own NP column); every disagreement
#     was adjudicated by a third, higher-magnification look.
#   - x_over_c was additionally checked against the SAME orifice coordinates printed on ten
#     OTHER, cleaner pages of the same report (the orifice X/L and Z/L are identical in every
#     M6 table; only CP changes with the test).
#   - every (x_over_c, Z/L) pair was checked against the independently committed, title-page
#     verified ONERA D section table models/onera_m6/agard_ar138_table_b1_1_section_coordinates.dat:
#     MEDIAN RESIDUAL 6.8e-05, MAXIMUM 5.9e-04 over all 271 rows, ZERO rows above 7e-04.
#   - THREE x_over_c values carry an UNRESOLVED 4th/5th decimal digit and are marked
#     'UNRESOLVED-XDIGIT' in the provenance file.  They are NOT marked in this data file because
#     the format has no comment column; the provenance file names them.  Cp is unaffected.
#   - NO Cp VALUE IS EMITTED THAT THE TWO INDEPENDENT READS DID NOT AGREE ON AFTER ADJUDICATION.
#
# NOTHING WAS SENT, FETCHED OR FILED.  The source PDF was already on this box.
#
# section  y_over_b  surface  x_over_c   Cp

